-- ============================================================================
-- gasvalue PROFESSIONAL DEEP SEED: Flare Gas to Value & LPG/CNG, intermediate
-- tier.
--
-- Six modules, 26 lessons, 132 questions (15 per module bank plus a 42
-- question final exam). The structure row is GENERATED from the tier's
-- manifest.json rather than hand typed.
--
-- What this tier owns: ROUTES, RECOVERY AND THE CREDIT. Four routes carry
-- requirement envelopes whose limits are the study's to set, and a check with
-- no limit is unchecked; each route's yield has a basis and a ceiling in what
-- the gas holds; a route's year is product, revenue, cost and margin per Mscf,
-- with a blank cost named and capital scaled by the modular power law and
-- handed on undiscounted; only the recovered share of the flare is avoided,
-- and the net abatement needs a declared counterfactual; the breakeven credit
-- price is closed form.
--
-- THE ENGINE FACT THIS TIER OWNS. One flare gives three different net
-- abatements under three counterfactuals, and the engine gives none until one
-- is declared.
--
-- THE TRAP THE TIER IS BUILT ON. The whole flare credited to a plant that
-- recovers part of it, the first clearing price in the order typed, and a yield
-- above what the gas holds each give a figure that looks finished.
--
-- HELD, taught as a limit and never graded: GWP values and credit prices as
-- case inputs (H4). Every figure is invented and illustrative. The capstone
-- grades six engine figures: capital at 0.01 dollars, two tonnages at 0.01 t,
-- the rest at 1e-4.
-- ============================================================================

